    <othernotes>Targeting notes for Juno:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Story: Juno is a human born on Mars of mixed Vietnamese and Chinese descent. She came to Earth due to her colony failing, and connected with Overwatch to both aid her home and to explore Earth. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Things to talk to Juno about!&lt;br&gt;-Martian: Juno is Martian, and considers that her primary identity, but she is human. She's happy to explore how alien this makes her, and she has a soft spot for old science fiction. Does this "Martian" measure up to expectations? What is her view of Earth and cultures?&lt;br&gt;-Tech: Juno's boots use a combination of thrusters and magnetics to keep her floating, but she's happy to be technical about other things, too. General technology questions about space, mining, geoengineering, and medicine are all good topics. &lt;br&gt;-Sheltered: Juno's got big homeschooled energy: She grew up in a pretty insulated environment. She isn't naive, but is a bit anxious about the world at large. Does her jitteryness frustrate your character? Does she seem like she's trying too hard? Maybe you want to ask her about things she's found interesting?&lt;br&gt;-Support: Juno is a bit of a swiss army knife. She has a lot of practical expertise, but prefers usually to not be the center of attention. Her primary abilities in Overwatch center on healing (or hurting) darts, healing (or hurting) rockets, and levitation. &lt;br&gt;-Body: Because she's grown up in a higher oxygen, lower gravity world, Juno has an unconventional body chemistry. Does this concern your character? Or do they like the idea of protecting her? ...Or just throwing her about in the bedroom?&lt;br&gt;-Scrappy: Mars has limited resources. What common things at the Inventory wow Juno, or would wow her from your character's world? What are some ways she's made life work with limited resources? &lt;br&gt;-Sex: Juno was born on Mars, and has a fairly excited view towards sexuality, but her exact experience level is deliberately left as something for other characters to explore.</othernotes>
